    {
      "id": "claim_7414caddf45c4549ae10dc50ac6b83c1",
      "statement": "reaper.py detects hung workers using a per-task max running time and an inactivity timeout: reap_active_workers terminates a worker that exceeded its budget and records the session end, and reap_stuck_tasks is the entry point the queue watchdog and the check-stuck CLI use; worker-failure handling is retry-oriented (a failed or vanished running worker returns to todo for re-spawn up to DEFAULT_MAX_WORKER_RETRIES), and the exhausted-retry path stamps blocked_reason_type='stuck' with assignee 'human'.",
